   "he": "טָבַל וְעָלָה הֲרֵי הוּא כְּיִשְׂרָאֵל לְכׇל דְּבָרָיו. לְמַאי הִלְכְתָא? דְּאִי הָדַר בֵּיהּ וּמְקַדֵּשׁ בַּת יִשְׂרָאֵל, יִשְׂרָאֵל מְשׁוּמָּד קָרֵינָא בֵּיהּ, וְקִידּוּשָׁיו קִידּוּשִׁין.",
   "en": "The baraita continues: Once «he has immersed and emerged he is a Jew in every sense.» The Gemara asks: «With regard to what halakha» is this said? It is «that if he reverts back» to behaving as a gentile, he nevertheless remains Jewish, «and» so if «he betroths a Jewish woman,» although «he is considered to be an apostate Jew, his betrothal is» a valid «betrothal.»"
  }
